Qore kalman Module Release Notes
================================

1.1
---
- Pre-baked model factories for common tracking cases: newConstantVelocity2D(),
  newConstantAcceleration2D(), newGpsSmoother(). Each returns a fully-configured
  LinearFilter ready to step — no manual F / H / Q / R construction needed for
  the 90% case.
- LinearFilter::stepBatch() — bulk predict+update across an observation list in
  one call, cheaper than N Qore round-trips. Checks for cooperative cancellation
  between iterations so long batches remain killable via cancel_thread() or
  SandboxManager::requestInterrupt().

1.0
---
- Initial public release.
- Matrix primitive (Eigen-backed) with arithmetic, transpose, inverse,
  cholesky, determinant. Immutable — every op returns a new Matrix.
- LinearFilter — standard linear Kalman filter (LKF).
- ExtendedFilter — extended Kalman filter (EKF); non-linear state-transition
  and observation functions supplied as Qore callbacks that also return the
  Jacobian.
- Joseph-form covariance update for numerical stability under accumulated
  floating-point error.
- Module version helpers: kalman_version(), get_kalman_info().

See the doxygen documentation (docs/release-notes.doxygen.tmpl, or the
generated HTML) for the in-tree canonical release notes.
